WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:03.747
AI can find the right sentence in a document,

00:00:03.747 --> 00:00:06.104
and still draw the wrong conclusion.

00:00:06.654 --> 00:00:09.966
That's the problem EvidenceTrail solves.

00:00:10.516 --> 00:00:14.500
Here's a real example from our recorded Meta Muse tests,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:16.492
using a fictional applicant.

00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:22.058
The job requires someone who personally negotiated supplier agreements.

00:00:22.608 --> 00:00:25.298
The CV mentions those agreements.

00:00:25.298 --> 00:00:26.846
But look carefully.

00:00:26.846 --> 00:00:31.900
The applicant says their procurement director negotiated them.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.568
The applicant only prepared comparison notes.

00:00:36.118 --> 00:00:38.201
Meta Muse identified a conflict.

00:00:38.201 --> 00:00:42.824
EvidenceTrail checked the original evidence, and corrected the finding:

00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:48.358
this CV does not establish that the applicant personally negotiated those agreements.

00:00:48.908 --> 00:00:50.966
We can inspect the source page,

00:00:50.966 --> 00:00:54.020
and see exactly where the quotation came from.

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:59.882
The source PDF shown is a documented reconstruction of the original test input,

00:00:59.882 --> 00:01:02.034
not the byte-identical original.

00:01:02.584 --> 00:01:07.048
And crucially, EvidenceTrail doesn't make hiring decisions.

00:01:07.598 --> 00:01:11.700
A human reviewer can request clarification and record a note,

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.390
without changing the underlying finding.

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:21.492
The result is a readable evidence report that makes the AI's interpretation transparent and reviewable.

00:01:22.042 --> 00:01:24.614
Meta Muse interprets.

00:01:24.614 --> 00:01:27.431
EvidenceTrail verifies.

00:01:27.431 --> 00:01:29.146
Humans decide.
